    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "READ BEFORE QUOTING A COST FIGURE.\n\nBILLED means Bifrost. The header TOTAL COST and TOTAL TOKENS come from bifrost.request.cost.usd and bifrost.tokens.total, tagged virtual_key_name:incident-response-agent-bfvk. The tag key is virtual_key_name -- virtual_key exists but is unpopulated (N/A only). Bifrost metrics carry NO incident id and NO sub-agent dimension, which is why every per-run and per-sub-agent number on this board comes from span data instead.\n\nESTIMATE means litellm list price. Every sub-agent cost figure is an estimate and says so in its column header. Bifrost bills per gateway request and cannot split one request across ~15 concurrent sub-agents, so a per-sub-agent billed number does not exist and cannot be made to exist. Billed and estimated will not reconcile, by construction -- ADO-200025 measured them ~15% apart on cost and ~57% apart on tokens over identical traffic. Never sum them together.\n\nRUN TOTALS ARE BILLED OR ABSENT. The litellm fallback for run totals was removed. A run Bifrost could not price has no iragent.cost_usd and no iragent.tokens at all, and its iragent.cost_source reads estimate_only. Check 'RUNS WITH NO BILLED COST' and the 'Run cost source' toplist before trusting a billed total -- those runs contribute nothing to it. ADO-200026 tracks the read-scoped /api/logs credential.\n\nml_obs.span.llm.total.cost is NANODOLLARS and is Datadog's own list-price reckoning, not an invoice. Every widget on it divides by 1e9 and says so.",
        "background_color": "yellow",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "vertical_align": "top",
        "show_tick": false,
        "has_padding": true
      },
      "layout": {
